## Accessibility Requirements

- Minimum contrast ratio: 4.5:1 for normal text
- Focus indicators: Always visible `focus:ring-2`
- Keyboard navigation: All interactive elements accessible
- Screen reader labels: Use aria-labels where needed
- Touch targets: Minimum 44x44px
- Color not sole indicator: Use icons + text

---

## Design Checklist for New Components

When creating new components, ensure:

Uses established color palette (indigo/purple/gray)
Follows responsive breakpoints (mobile-first)
Implements proper hover/focus states
Uses consistent spacing (4, 6, 8 scale)
Includes loading and error states
Has proper typography hierarchy
Uses appropriate shadows and borders
Follows established border-radius standards
Includes status indicators with colors + icons
Is accessible (keyboard, screen reader, contrast)

---

## Usage Instructions

**When developing new features:**
1. Copy relevant sections from this design system
2. Maintain color consistency (indigo/purple primary)
3. Use established component patterns
4. Follow responsive guidelines
5. Test on mobile, tablet, and desktop
6. Ensure accessibility standards are met

**Example Prompt for New Feature:**
"Create a [feature name] using the School Management System design system. Use the indigo-600 to purple-600 gradient for primary elements, gray-50 for backgrounds, maintain responsive breakpoints (sm, md, lg), follow the card style (bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm p-6), and ensure mobile-first responsive design."

